# component-src.pkg -- the SOURCE half of a component, and why it is not a
# courtesy.
#
# The BINARY packages create licence obligations, and a source package is how
# they are satisfied.  What ships in one image of ours:
#
#	runtime   rcs, under the GNU GPL VERSION 1 (all 19 files say so and
#	          "version 2" appears nowhere in the directory)
#	archive   gzip, GPLv2
#	games     tetris, distributable only "without any fee or other monetary
#	          gains", authorship statement reproduced on all copies
#	net       GNU screen, GPL VERSION 1 -- its COPYING is the v1 text and all
#	          11 sources say "either version 1".
#	mgr       Bellcore's grant: no sale for profit, and "the copyright notice
#	          must be reproduced on copies"
#
# So a source package that omitted what the licence requires would be worse than
# none: it reads as the obligation having been discharged.  WHICH components are
# under which terms is dist/licences.tab, and a component whose terms oblige
# source declares the `src' kind so this package is cut.  THE RULE APPLIED,
# stated so a reader can check it rather than trust it:
#
#   FOR EVERY EXECUTABLE THE SIBLING -bin PACKAGE INSTALLS, this package carries
#   the complete corresponding source for that executable, the recipe that
#   compiles it, and every licence text that governs that source.  Not the
#   component's `.c' files -- the SOURCE ROOT, so a COPYING sitting beside them
#   travels with them; and not the whole producing repository either, because a
#   package that ships everything says nothing about what this component needed.
#
# The mapping from a shipped program to its sources is the BUILD's (one
# directory is not one program: base/cmd/diff builds diff and diffh,
# base/cmd/knapsack builds enroll, xencode and xdecode and no `knapsack'), so it
# is read from the map the build itself records -- hostbuild/ulsrcmap.py writes
# hostbuild/build/.ulsrcmap -- and never guessed at.  `component.py component
# <name> src' REFUSES while any executable is unmapped, and names them.  That refusal is the gate for the rule above:
# coverage is not partial here, it is all or nothing.
#
# The count is recorded rather than recomputed: `programs' is how many
# executables the -bin half installs and `mapped' is how many this package
# answers for.  They must be equal, and `keymatch' below is what says so from
# inside the archive, so an operator who has only the source package can still
# see that it is complete.
#
# `toolchain_src' in .provenance names the toolchain's own -src package: every
# program here links its csu and compiles against its headers, and the
# toolchain ships that source itself (ulsrcmap.py, ELSEWHERE) rather than this
# package carrying paths a release-shaped toolchain checkout may not have
# unpacked.  This package is the complete corresponding source only alongside
# the package that field names.
kind      component-src
what      one component's complete corresponding source, its recipe and its licences
producer  dist/pack-component.sh
archive   c900-@C@-src-v@V@.tar.gz
toplevel  c900-@C@-src-v@V@
version   VERSION
stamp     .provenance  kind commit version package component pkgkind entries programs mapped contentid
text      .provenance  ^package=@C@-src$
text      .provenance  ^pkgkind=src$
text      .provenance  ^component=@C@$
# Every executable accounted for, asserted from the package's own stamp.  A
# source package that covers 40 of a component's 50 programs states an
# obligation it has not discharged, and this is the line that refuses it.
keymatch  .provenance programs  .provenance mapped
file      LICENSE
# ---- THE TERMS THE CONTENTS ARE UNDER ----
# LICENSE above is what this repository says about its OWN files.  What the
# component's CONTENTS are under travels with the release, not inside each
# archive: the texts are collected once into `licences' beside the packages,
# with an index.tab saying which regimes govern which component.  A source
# package carries each program's own COPYING beside the code as well, because
# it ships the source root upstream put it in.
file      manifest.tab
dir       files
glob      files/*  1
text      manifest.tab  ^f .
# ---- WHICH BYTES ----
# Source is text, so unlike a compiler its bytes ARE a stable name for it: a
# content id is recomputable here and is recorded, and any consumer verifies
# it directly with `md5sum -c .contents'.  See component-bin.pkg.
file      .contents
idfile    .contents  .provenance  contentid
